{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "counters-piggyback-serialized-block",
    "parent": "fault-counter-readout-plumbing",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Emit fault/recovery counters as fields inside deliveryEffects, the one block proven to reach the evaluation record",
    "description": "Subject-side readout fix, no harness change. In spur/spur-core/src/simulator/util_stats.rs add flat default-0 u64 fields to the existing DeliveryEffects struct (serialized as `deliveryEffects`, which IS present in every recent evaluation record): crashes_total, crashes_with_own_sends_inflight, recoveries_total, recoveries_with_own_prior_sends_inflight, stale_sender_deliveries_after_recovery. Increment at the existing crash/recover/delivery sites under the already-live `stats`/`emit_acted_fraction` gate; no new config key, no scheduling change. DROP the proposed generic probe_a..probe_d scratch quartet: undeclared always-zero fields are exactly what dead-counter-audit-invariant exists to reject, and speculative fields cannot be attributed to a mechanism. Implementation step 1 is the verification run: one short session, confirm the new fields appear in the eval record's utilStats.deliveryEffects. If they do not appear, the projection is an allow-list at FIELD granularity, and that negative closes both fault-counter-readout-plumbing and orchestrator-util-subset-passthrough as subject-side options and must be surfaced to the operator rather than patched around (rule 9 forbids touching the orchestrator).",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "util_stats",
      "deliveryEffects serialization",
      "crash/recover fault injection"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 6,
    "expectedCost": 1.5,
    "rationale": "Three consecutive iterations (stale-delivery-expedite, prefix-extension-policy-depth-diagnostic, coverage-guided-fault-placement) each burned a full sequential screen and returned an uninterpretable null purely because their fire-criterion counters never reached the evaluation record — the 2026-08-30 log records that emit_prefix_extension is ALREADY true at session level in general_vr.json and the prefixExtension block still does not appear in either seed's utilStats, and that fault_coverage.* was likewise absent. Every gated fault/recovery hypothesis in the pool (including two below) is unscoreable until this is fixed. Piggybacking on a block with demonstrated serialization is the only in-bounds channel. It also delivers the rule-8 base rates for the two predicates the deep-fault family depends on at zero marginal cost.",
    "generalityArgument": "Counts crash, recovery, incarnation and pending-send events from the simulator's own vocabulary. No handler, message type, timer label or role appears; identical for VR, Mencius or any future spec, and degenerate (all zero) on fault-free specs.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-30T03:20:00.000Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "Red team: this may fail in exactly the way its predecessors did — if the record's utilStats is filtered by an explicit field allow-list rather than a block allow-list, new deliveryEffects fields will be dropped too and the patch buys nothing but a negative. That negative is still the cheapest available and is the deliverable. Second risk: enabling merges with no code effect have merged on test artifacts alone before (see enabling-merge-requires-nonempty-code-diff); demand the verification-run JSON, not a passing unit test. FALSIFIER: run one short session post-patch and grep the evaluation record for utilStats.deliveryEffects.crashes_total; absent => hypothesis refuted and the subject-side readout family closes."
  },
